frame(g = [1, 2], x = [1.0, 2]).aggregate(y = x + 1, by: g)
---
error[Z0401]: `y` of `aggregate` gives a Column, not one value per group
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:47
  |
1 | frame(g = [1, 2], x = [1.0, 2]).aggregate(y = x + 1, by: g)
  |                                               ^^^^^ a Column
  |
  = help: a definition reduces the group to one value, as `mean(wage)` or `sd(wage) / sqrt(n())` do; `add` keeps a value per row

